    "title": "A new travel center is opening at the gateway to Yosemite - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Christian Valdez No media credit provided. ,\n4 hours ago MADERA, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) – A Yosemite Travel Center at Tesoro Viejo is opening on July 2 in Madera County.\nThe new development is at Highway 41 and Tesoro Viejo Blvd and Avenue 15, according to Madera County officials. The center includes a gas station with six pumps, a convenience market, a Jamba Juice, and a car wash.\nOfficials describe Madera County as the gateway to Yosemite, adding that a facility like this can benefit the people who live in the area as well as the tourists who travel through the park.\nThe facility will officially open on Thursday with a ribbon-cutting ceremony.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS47 and KSEE24 | News from YourCentralValley.com.",
    "summary": "The new development is at Highway 41 and Tesoro Viejo Blvd and Avenue 15, according to Madera County officials. The center includes a gas station with six pumps, a convenience market, a Jamba Juice, and a car wash. Officials describe Madera County as the gateway to Yosemite, adding that a facility like this can benefit the people who live in the area as well as the tourists who travel through the park. The facility will officially open on Thursday with a ribbon-cutting ceremony. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
